--
An explicit/pseudo destructor call written with a template-id
(`p->~Foo<T>()`) names Foo<T>'s destructor; the template arguments are not a
template-id to instantiate ([expr.prim.id.dtor], [class.dtor]).  CBMC must
not try to instantiate `~Foo` as a template.  This is the form used by
libstdc++'s _Rb_tree::_M_construct_node.
